## DESCRIPTION
## Find the inverse of a 2 by 2 matrix.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## KEYWORDS('matrix inverse')

## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Matrices)
## DBsection(Inverses)
## Date(September 5, 2008)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)

# updated 2023.11.10

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',             'PGML.pl',
    'parserRadioMultiAnswer.pl', 'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context('Matrix');

do {
    $A = Matrix([ map { [ map { random(-6, 6) } (1 .. 2) ] } (1 .. 2) ]);
} until abs($A->det) > 1 && abs($A->det) <= 5;

$Ainv = $A->inverse;

$rma = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ["The matrix \( A^{-1}\) doesn't exist"],
        [ 'The matrix \( A^{-1} = \) %s*', $Ainv ]
    ],
    1
);

BEGIN_PGML
Let [```A = [$A]```]

[_]{$rma}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Since [`A`] is a 2 by 2 matrix, we can use the inverse formula for this for 
[``` A = \begin{bmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{bmatrix} ```]
First, the
determinant is [`|A| = a d - bc = [$A->det] `] and then
[``` A^{-1} = \frac{1}{|A|} \begin{bmatrix} d & - b \\ -c & a \end{bmatrix} 
= [$Ainv] ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
